module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Finite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FittingIdeal

/-!
# Sections of a module over an étale chart, and base change along a chart morphism

Let `F` be an algebraic space and let `G` be an `𝒪_F`-module on the small étale site of `F`.
For an étale chart `U` of `F` the sections `𝒪_F(U)` form a commutative ring and the sections
`G(U)` form a module over it, and a morphism `f : V ⟶ U` of charts restricts sections along the
ring map `𝒪_F(U) → 𝒪_F(V)`.  Because that restriction is semilinear, it has a canonical
`𝒪_F(V)`-linear extension

`𝒪_F(V) ⊗_{𝒪_F(U)} G(U) ⟶ G(V)`,

the *base change comparison* over `f`.  This file constructs that comparison and records the
consequence the Fitting-ideal sheaf of Stacks 0CZ5 needs: wherever the comparison is bijective,
restriction carries the chartwise Fitting ideal of Stacks 07ZA onto the chartwise Fitting ideal
over the smaller chart.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing` is the ring `𝒪_F(U)` of sections of the structure sheaf
  over an étale chart, with `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing_commRing` its commutativity and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrict` the restriction ring map along a chart morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlgebra` is the resulting `𝒪_F(U)`-algebra structure on
  `𝒪_F(V)`, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsModule` the resulting `𝒪_F(U)`-module
  structure on `G(V)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrictLinear` is the restriction of sections as an
  `𝒪_F(U)`-linear map `G(U) →ₗ G(V)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionsBaseChange` is the base change comparison
  `𝒪_F(V) ⊗_{𝒪_F(U)} G(U) →ₗ[𝒪_F(V)] G(V)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineCharts` says that the comparison is bijective for
  every morphism between affine étale charts.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartBaseChange_tmul` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartBaseChange_one_tmul` evaluate the comparison, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.range_chartBaseChange` computes its range as the `𝒪_F(V)`-span of the
  restricted sections, whence
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bijective_chartBaseChange_id`: the comparison over an identity chart
  morphism is bijective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finite_sections_of_surjective_chartBaseChange` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.module_finite_sections_of_bijective_chartBaseChange`: where the
  comparison is surjective, finiteness of the sections propagates to the smaller chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_map_le_of_surjective_chartBaseChange`: where the
  comparison is surjective, restriction carries `Fit_r(G(U))` into `Fit_r(G(V))`.  This is the
  sub-presheaf property of the chartwise Fitting ideals.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange`: where the comparison is bijective,
  `Fit_r(G(V))` is the ideal generated by the image of `Fit_r(G(U))` under restriction.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts` is the
  same conclusion from `IsCartesianOnAffineCharts`.

## Implementation notes

The structure sheaf of the small étale ringed site is the `RingCat`-valued
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringSheaf`, so commutativity has to be recovered before an ideal
or a tensor product can be formed.  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing_commRing` recovers it by
extending the `RingCat`-level `Ring` instance by the commutativity of the `CommRingCat`-valued
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureSheaf`, rather than by transporting the whole `CommRing`
structure across the two spellings: the `Ring` field of the resulting instance is then
*syntactically* the one the `ModuleCat`-valued sections are modules over, which is what keeps
`Module (chartRing …) (G.val.obj …)` solvable by instance search.

`chartAlgebra` and `chartSectionsModule` depend on the chart morphism, so they cannot be
instances; they are `@[instance_reducible]` definitions, to be introduced by `letI` at each use,
as in the statements below.  With these in scope the comparison is Mathlib's
`LinearMap.liftBaseChange`, and the tensor product is `TensorProduct (chartRing … U)
(chartRing … V) (G.val.obj (op U))`, the same spelling as in the base change clause of
`fittingIdeal_basic_properties`, so that clause applies with no transport.

Nothing here derives the bijectivity of the comparison from quasi-coherence of `G`.  That
implication is Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) (equivalently Étale Cohomology, Theorem 03OJ) for
the chart `U`, which identifies quasi-coherent modules on the small étale site of a *scheme*
with quasi-coherent modules on the scheme; `SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite` as defined in
this repository is a purely local condition — every object of the site has *a* covering on whose
members the module has a global presentation — and passing from it to a statement about the
sections over one affine chart is the content of Descent, Proposition 03DX(2), which is not
available here.  So `IsCartesianOnAffineCharts` is carried as a hypothesis.

**The passage does not need Descent, Proposition 03DW (vanishing of higher étale cohomology of
a quasi-coherent module on an affine scheme).**  The Stacks proof
of 03DX cites 03DV, 0GN7, 023T, 03DL and 03EM, and does *not* cite 03DW; neither does 03DV's proof
(03DL, 01BE, 03DN) nor 0GN7's (03DU, 03DV, 03FH, 03FE).  03DW is a later proposition whose own
proof routes through 03F9/03FJ/03F7/01XD/013P — it is a *consumer* of this area, not an input to
it.  What the implication actually needs is 03DT (the fpqc sheaf condition for the cartesian
presheaf of a module), together with flatness of the chart restrictions
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine`), a finite affine refinement of an étale
covering of an affine chart, and the sheaf condition.  Given 03DT the cohomology vanishing comes
out *derived* rather than assumed.

Affineness of the *smaller* chart `V` is necessary and not a convenience: for `U = Spec k[x, y]`,
`V = U ∖ {(x, y)}` (étale over `U`, not affine) and `G` the module of sections of
`𝒪_U/(x, y)`, one has `G(V) = 0` while `𝒪_F(V) ⊗_{𝒪_F(U)} G(U) = k`.  This is why
`IsCartesianOnAffineCharts` quantifies over affine `U` *and* affine `V`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CZ5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CZ5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u m

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)

/-! ### The ring of sections over a chart -/

/-- The ring `𝒪_F(U)` of sections of the structure sheaf of the small étale site of `F` over an
étale chart `U`. -/
noncomputable abbrev chartRing (U : SmallEtale B S hS F) : Type u :=
  ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O)).obj.obj (op U)

/-- The sections of the structure sheaf over a chart form a *commutative* ring: the
`RingCat`-valued structure sheaf of the small étale ringed site is the `CommRingCat`-valued
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureSheaf` with its commutativity forgotten.

Only `mul_comm` is added to the ambient `Ring` instance, so that instance remains syntactically
the one over which the module sections of an `𝒪_F`-module are modules. -/
noncomputable instance chartRing_commRing (U : SmallEtale B S hS F) :
    CommRing (chartRing B S hS F hF U) :=
  letI r : Ring (chartRing B S hS F hF U) := inferInstance
  { r with
    mul_comm := by
      change ∀ a b : (structureSheaf B S hS F hF).obj.obj (op U), a * b = b * a
      exact fun a b => mul_comm a b }

variable {B S hS F hF}

/-- Restriction of regular functions along a morphism `f : V ⟶ U` of étale charts of `F`. -/
noncomputable abbrev chartRestrict {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    chartRing B S hS F hF U →+* chartRing B S hS F hF V :=
  (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O)).obj.map f.op).hom

/-- Restriction along the identity morphism of a chart is the identity ring homomorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem chartRestrict_id (U : SmallEtale B S hS F) :
    chartRestrict (hF := hF) (𝟙 U) = RingHom.id (chartRing B S hS F hF U) :=
  congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O).obj.map_id
      (op U))

/-- Restriction along a composite `g ≫ f` of chart morphisms is restriction along `f` followed by
restriction along `g`. -/
theorem chartRestrict_comp {U V W : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) (g : W ⟶ V) :
    chartRestrict (hF := hF) (g ≫ f) =
      (chartRestrict (hF := hF) g).comp (chartRestrict (hF := hF) f) :=
  congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O).obj.map_comp
      f.op g.op)

/-- The `𝒪_F(U)`-algebra structure on `𝒪_F(V)` given by restriction along a chart morphism
`f : V ⟶ U`.  Not an instance: it depends on `f`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def chartAlgebra {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    Algebra (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V) :=
  (chartRestrict f).toAlgebra

/-- The structure map of `chartAlgebra f` is the restriction `chartRestrict f`. -/
theorem chartAlgebra_algebraMap {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    algebraMap (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V) = chartRestrict f := rfl

/-! ### Sections of a module over a chart -/

/-- The `𝒪_F(U)`-module structure on the sections `G(V)` over a smaller chart, given by
restriction of scalars along `f : V ⟶ U`.  Not an instance: it depends on `f`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def chartSectionsModule (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    Module (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op V)) :=
  Module.compHom _ (chartRestrict f)

/-- Under `chartSectionsModule G f`, a scalar `r` of `𝒪_F(U)` acts on `G(V)` as its restriction
`chartRestrict f r`. -/
theorem chartSectionsModule_smul (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    (r : chartRing B S hS F hF U) (x : G.val.obj (op V)) :
    letI := chartSectionsModule G f
    r • x = chartRestrict (hF := hF) f r • x := rfl

/-- Restriction along a chart morphism is compatible with the two scalar actions. -/
theorem chartSections_isScalarTower (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    letI := chartSectionsModule G f
    IsScalarTower (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (G.val.obj (op V)) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule G f
  exact IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul (fun _ _ => rfl)

/-- Restriction of sections of an `𝒪_F`-module along a chart morphism, as an `𝒪_F(U)`-linear
map. -/
noncomputable def chartRestrictLinear (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    letI := chartSectionsModule G f
    (G.val.obj (op U) : Type m) →ₗ[chartRing B S hS F hF U] (G.val.obj (op V) : Type m) :=
  (G.val.map f.op).hom

/-- The linear map `chartRestrictLinear G f` is the restriction map `G(U) ⟶ G(V)` of `G`. -/
theorem chartRestrictLinear_apply (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) (x : G.val.obj (op U)) :
    chartRestrictLinear G f x = (G.val.map f.op) x := rfl

/-! ### The base change comparison -/

/-- The base change comparison over a morphism `f : V ⟶ U` of étale charts of `F`: the
`𝒪_F(V)`-linear extension `𝒪_F(V) ⊗_{𝒪_F(U)} G(U) ⟶ G(V)` of the restriction of sections.

Its bijectivity for `U` and `V` affine is the comparison of Stacks 03DX(2); it is not proved
here, see the implementation notes. -/
noncomputable def sectionsBaseChange (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (G.val.obj (op U)) →ₗ[
        chartRing B S hS F hF V] (G.val.obj (op V) : Type m) :=
  letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  letI := chartSectionsModule G f
  haveI := chartSections_isScalarTower G f
  LinearMap.liftBaseChange _ (chartRestrictLinear G f)

/-- The base change comparison sends `b ⊗ x` to `b • chartRestrictLinear G f x`. -/
theorem chartBaseChange_tmul (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    (b : chartRing B S hS F hF V) (x : G.val.obj (op U)) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    sectionsBaseChange G f (TensorProduct.tmul _ b x) = b • chartRestrictLinear G f x := rfl

/-- The base change comparison sends `1 ⊗ x` to the restriction `chartRestrictLinear G f x`. -/
theorem chartBaseChange_one_tmul (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) (x : G.val.obj (op U)) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    sectionsBaseChange G f (TensorProduct.tmul _ (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF V) x) =
      chartRestrictLinear G f x := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  exact one_smul (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (chartRestrictLinear G f x)

/-- The image of the base change comparison is the `𝒪_F(V)`-submodule generated by the
restricted sections. -/
theorem range_chartBaseChange (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    LinearMap.range (sectionsBaseChange G f) =
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (Set.range fun x : G.val.obj (op U) => chartRestrictLinear G f x) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule G f
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower G f
  exact LinearMap.range_liftBaseChange _ (chartRestrictLinear G f)

/-- The base change comparison is surjective exactly when the restricted sections generate the
sections over the smaller chart. -/
theorem chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U) :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange G f) ↔
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (Set.range fun x : G.val.obj (op U) => chartRestrictLinear G f x) = ⊤ := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  rw [← LinearMap.range_eq_top, range_chartBaseChange]

/-- Restriction of sections along the identity morphism of a chart is the identity. -/
theorem chartRestrictLinear_id (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (U : SmallEtale B S hS F)
    (x : G.val.obj (op U)) : chartRestrictLinear G (𝟙 U) x = x :=
  congrArg (fun φ => (ConcreteCategory.hom φ) x) (G.val.presheaf.map_id (op U))

/-- The base change comparison over an identity chart morphism is bijective: `𝒪_F(U)`-sections
base changed along the identity of `𝒪_F(U)` are the `𝒪_F(U)`-sections.

This is the degenerate case of the comparison, and it says that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionsBaseChange` is normalized correctly. -/
theorem bijective_chartBaseChange_id (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS F) : Function.Bijective (sectionsBaseChange G (𝟙 U)) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) (𝟙 U)
  let _ := chartSectionsModule G (𝟙 U)
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower G (𝟙 U)
  have hleft : ∀ z : TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF U)
      (G.val.obj (op U)),
      TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)
        (sectionsBaseChange G (𝟙 U) z) = z := by
    intro z
    induction z using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero =>
      exact (congrArg (TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U)
        (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)) (map_zero _)).trans (TensorProduct.tmul_zero _ _)
    | tmul b y =>
      have hb : b • (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U) = b :=
        (by simp : chartRestrict (hF := hF) (𝟙 U) b * 1 = b)
      calc TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)
            (sectionsBaseChange G (𝟙 U) (TensorProduct.tmul _ b y))
          = TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)
              (b • chartRestrictLinear G (𝟙 U) y) :=
            congrArg _ (chartBaseChange_tmul G (𝟙 U) b y)
        _ = TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)
              (b • y) := by rw [chartRestrictLinear_id]
        _ = TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U)
              (b • (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)) y :=
            (TensorProduct.smul_tmul b (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U) y).symm
        _ = TensorProduct.tmul _ b y := by rw [hb]
    | add z w hz hw =>
      exact (congrArg (TensorProduct.tmul (chartRing B S hS F hF U)
        (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF U)) (map_add _ z w)).trans
        ((TensorProduct.tmul_add _ _ _).trans (congrArg₂ (· + ·) hz hw))
  exact ⟨Function.LeftInverse.injective hleft, fun y =>
    ⟨_, (chartBaseChange_one_tmul G (𝟙 U) y).trans (chartRestrictLinear_id G U y)⟩⟩

/-- An `𝒪_F`-module is *cartesian on affine charts* when for every morphism of affine étale
charts of `F` the base change comparison is bijective, that is, when the sections over the
smaller chart are the base change of the sections over the larger one.

For a quasi-coherent module this is Stacks 03DX(2) applied to the larger chart; see the
implementation notes for why it is a hypothesis here rather than a consequence. -/
def IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) : Prop :=
  ∀ (U V : SmallEtale B S hS F),
    IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U) →
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V) →
        ∀ f : V ⟶ U, Function.Bijective (sectionsBaseChange G f)

/-! ### Fitting ideals of the sections over a chart -/

/-- The chartwise Fitting ideal of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart` is the
module-theoretic Fitting ideal of the sections over the chart, in the commutative ring structure
of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing_commRing`. -/
theorem fittingIdealOnChart_eq_fittingIdeal (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (r : ℕ)
    (U : SmallEtale B S hS F)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))] :
    fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r U =
      _root_.fittingIdeal (R := chartRing B S hS F hF U)
        (M := G.val.obj (op U)) (r : ℤ) := rfl

/-- Where the base change comparison over `f : V ⟶ U` is surjective, finiteness of the sections
over `U` gives finiteness of the sections over `V`. -/
theorem module_finite_sections_of_surjective_chartBaseChange
    (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))]
    (hf : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange G f)) :
    Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (G.val.obj (op V)) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule G f
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower G f
  exact Module.Finite.of_surjective (sectionsBaseChange G f) hf

/-- Where the base change comparison over `f : V ⟶ U` is bijective, finiteness of the sections
over `U` gives finiteness of the sections over `V`. -/
theorem module_finite_sections_of_bijective_chartBaseChange
    (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))]
    (hf : Function.Bijective (sectionsBaseChange G f)) :
    Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (G.val.obj (op V)) :=
  module_finite_sections_of_surjective_chartBaseChange G f hf.2

/-- Restriction carries the chartwise Fitting ideal over `U` onto the Fitting ideal of the base
change `𝒪_F(V) ⊗_{𝒪_F(U)} G(U)`. -/
private theorem map_fittingIdealOnChart_eq_fittingIdeal_tensor
    (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (r : ℕ) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))] :
    letI := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    Ideal.map (chartRestrict f) (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r U) =
      _root_.fittingIdeal (R := chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (M := TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
          (G.val.obj (op U))) (r : ℤ) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  exact ((fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, m, m, u} (R := chartRing B S hS F hF U)
    (M := G.val.obj (op U))).2.2.1 _ r).symm

/-- Where the base change comparison over `f : V ⟶ U` is merely surjective — that is, where the
sections over `U` generate the sections over `V` — the image of the `r`-th chartwise Fitting
ideal over `U` under restriction is already contained in the `r`-th chartwise Fitting ideal
over `V`.

This containment is the sub-presheaf property of the chartwise Fitting ideals, which is what
makes the Fitting ideal sheaf of Stacks 0CZ5 well defined; the reverse containment needs
injectivity of the comparison, see
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange`. -/
theorem fittingIdealOnChart_map_le_of_surjective_chartBaseChange
    (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (r : ℕ)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))]
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (G.val.obj (op V))]
    (hf : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange G f)) :
    Ideal.map (chartRestrict f) (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r U) ≤
      fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r V := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule G f
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower G f
  rw [map_fittingIdealOnChart_eq_fittingIdeal_tensor G r f]
  exact (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, max u m, m, u}
    (R := chartRing B S hS F hF V)
    (M := TensorProduct (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (G.val.obj (op U)))).2.2.2.2.1 _ (sectionsBaseChange G f) r hf

/-- Where the base change comparison over `f : V ⟶ U` is bijective, the `r`-th chartwise Fitting
ideal over `V` is generated by the image of the `r`-th chartwise Fitting ideal over `U` under
restriction.

This is the base change clause of `fittingIdeal_basic_properties` (Stacks 07ZA) transported to
the sections of an `𝒪_F`-module, and it is the comparison the Fitting ideal sheaf of
Stacks 0CZ5 needs in order to be a sheaf of ideals. -/
theorem fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (r : ℕ)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (f : V ⟶ U)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))]
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (G.val.obj (op V))]
    (hf : Function.Bijective (sectionsBaseChange G f)) :
    fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r V =
      Ideal.map (chartRestrict f) (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r U) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule G f
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower G f
  let e := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (sectionsBaseChange G f) hf
  exact (fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv e r).symm.trans
    (map_fittingIdealOnChart_eq_fittingIdeal_tensor G r f).symm

/-- For a module cartesian on affine charts, restriction between affine étale charts carries the
chartwise Fitting ideal onto the chartwise Fitting ideal. -/
theorem fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts
    (G : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hG : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts G) (r : ℕ)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hU : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V))
    (f : V ⟶ U)
    [Module.Finite (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (G.val.obj (op U))] :
    letI := module_finite_sections_of_bijective_chartBaseChange G f (hG U V hU hV f)
    fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r V =
      Ideal.map (chartRestrict f) (fittingIdealOnChart B S hS F hF G r U) := by
  have _ := module_finite_sections_of_bijective_chartBaseChange G f (hG U V hU hV f)
  exact fittingIdealOnChart_baseChange G r f (hG U V hU hV f)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

